$ cc-share install 0 --no-announce --no-autostart
sharing as user tester on HOSTNAME: ports 3400 
firewall: to open the pairing and paired-Frame ports (3399-3449) for your private networks, so the Frame can reach this machine, run these (or pass --yes):
  sudo ufw allow proto tcp from 10.0.0.0/8 to any port 3399:3449 comment 'Command Center'
  sudo ufw allow proto tcp from 172.16.0.0/12 to any port 3399:3449 comment 'Command Center'
  sudo ufw allow proto tcp from 192.168.0.0/16 to any port 3399:3449 comment 'Command Center'
not announcing
checklist:
  ok   krdpserver
  ok   kscreen-doctor
  ok   avahi-publish
  need the firewall to let the Frame in (ports 3399-3449, private ranges only): cc-share fix
  ok   cc-host (cc-host VERSION): the agent, pairing and tag screens
  need control-center-agent: systemctl --user status control-center-agent
  need control-center-guard: systemctl --user status control-center-guard
  need the agent on 3399: journalctl --user -u control-center-agent
  ok   krdp certificate
  note host id: made at the first pairing
  note not announcing: the Frame won't list this machine (cc-share announce on), its address can still be typed
  ok   starts from the app menu / taskbar: Command Center Host (cc-share autostart on: at login)
  note linger off: the units run while you're logged in (loginctl enable-linger to run them without)
  note shared login (slot 0) still active on monitor 0: anyone with its password can connect
some items need you (above)

Next, pair this machine with the Frame:
  1. Here, run: cc-share pair
     A 6-digit key fills the screen for 5 minutes.
  2. On the Frame, open Workspace, then Machines, then Add machine. Pick HOSTNAME, press Pair,
     and type the key, or press Pair by looking and look at this screen.
  The Frame only lists this machine while it announces itself: cc-share announce on
[exit 0]
